{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfpmmigR422hPCoAYsaqh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Worth separating, because I think they have different answers and the second one is where most of the disagreement lives.\n\n**On \"done.\"** The definition I'd defend is: the scope is covered, the behavior is *verified by running it*, and the remaining gaps are written down somewhere other than my head. The middle clause is the one that fails most often. There's a real difference between \"I ran `npm test` and got 6 tests, 1 pass, 5 fail, all failing with `TypeError: slugify is not a function`\" and \"I wrote tests that should fail.\" The first is a result; the second is an inference wearing a result's clothes. A lot of work that gets reported as done is the second kind, and it's invisible until someone else runs it.\n\nThe third clause matters because it's what keeps \"done with caveats\" from quietly becoming \"done.\" The slugify work right now is *not* done — it's tests-only, by your instruction — and the underscore and Unicode questions are gaps. If those lived only in my working memory, you'd have a work item that looks finished and isn't.\n\n**On the judgment call.** The usual discriminators don't survive contact:\n\n*Confidence* is the wrong axis. I was quite confident about what most slugify libraries do with underscores — they keep them. High confidence, but it still wasn't my call, because confidence is about knowing the answer and this was about having the authority to pick one. Those come apart constantly.\n\n*Spec silence* is too common to be a trigger. ISSUE.md was silent on test naming, file layout, assertion style, whether to use `node:test`. Silence is the normal condition. If silence meant ask, nothing would ever ship.\n\nWhat I'd actually use is two questions. First: **is this a fact or a preference?** Whether `[^a-z0-9]` matches `é` is a fact — I can test it in ten seconds, and asking you would be a failure of effort. Whether `é` *should* become `e`, stay `é`, or vanish is a preference about product behavior, and no amount of reading the repo settles it.\n\nSecond, for preferences only: **would being wrong announce itself, and would it be cheap to undo?** These are separate, and that's the part I think gets collapsed. If I guess wrong and a test goes red in thirty seconds, guessing is correct — the feedback loop *is* the judgment mechanism, and asking just burns a round trip. Underscores fail both tests: slugs become URLs, URLs get indexed and bookmarked, and the wrongness surfaces months later as broken links. Meanwhile a force-push is noticed instantly and is still irreversible, so detectability alone isn't enough.\n\n**The interaction between the two halves is the dangerous part.** An unresolved judgment call creates pressure to redefine done around it — \"I wasn't sure about Unicode, so I scoped it out and finished the rest.\" That produces the worst artifact available: something that looks complete and has a hole in it. The discipline is to finish everything that doesn't depend on the open question, then name the question. Shrinking the scope is your decision, not mine.\n\nTwo things I'd push back on in the framing. This sounds like a gate at the *end* of a work item, but the cost of asking is roughly flat while the cost of a wrong guess compounds with everything built on top of it — so these belong in the middle, before the dependent work exists. And any heuristic here is gameable in both directions: ask about everything and you've just handed the work back; ask about nothing and you ship confident wrongness. It only works if the default is decide-it-myself and asking has to clear a bar.\n\nWhere I'm less sure: how much of this you'd want *stated* versus just done. I could have picked underscores-stay, noted it in one line, and kept going — you'd have had working code and a flag to override. Would you rather I bias toward that, and reserve actual stopping for things like destructive operations?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10269,"cache_read_input_tokens":12801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10269},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60646288-b4f0-413f-a72a-55878a7be12e","uuid":"81e18b03-dceb-4c1b-a422-61b966ff9fd4","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:31:33.441Z","request_id":"req_011CfpmmiTXKsXjLFULP77Um"}
